# Billing Service Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and update with your actual values

## Core Infrastructure
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3004

## Database
# Least-privilege application role (NOSUPERUSER, NOBYPASSRLS, non-owner) so RLS enforces.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://telemetry_app:telemetry_app_local_dev@localhost:5432/telemetry

## Cache
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

## Observability
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
LOG_LEVEL=debug

## Security (SENSITIVE - change in production)
# Shared service-to-service secret. Required: startup fails, with the field named, if it is
# missing or under 32 characters once leading/trailing whitespace is stripped (the schema trims
# before measuring). Guards billing's internal route group -- POST /v1/internal/billing/generate
# today -- against in-cluster callers and the published 3004 port mapping. The gateway proxies
# /v1/billing to the same prefix upstream, so it does not reach that route today.
#
# Rotate this on every service at once. It is shared with gateway, usage-service and
# worker-service, and since T-044 a value billing rejects stops billing booting rather than
# letting it start and fail requests -- so a partial rotation surfaces at a different service
# from the one you edited.
#
# Measured on this host (fastify 5.10.0, undici 7.29.0 and a raw socket, four padding forms):
# space- and tab-padded header values arrive already stripped, so ordinary padding is harmless.
# A value padded with a non-breaking space (U+00A0) survives the wire and, because the configured
# secret is trimmed, no longer matches -- a 401, not a silent acceptance. Paste plain text.
INTERNAL_API_SECRET=dev-local-secret-change-in-production
